## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design a compliant, scalable data lifecycle with multi-tenant isolation, clear ownership, and automated governance in a dbt/Snowflake environment.

## Key Concepts
- dbt macros and run-operations for lifecycle management
- Snowflake Tasks and time-based scheduling
- Per-tenant Row-Level Security (RLS) isolation
- Data governance and CI gates for lifecycle policies

## Code Example
```sql
{% macro apply_retention(tenant, table) %}
  {% set policy = ref('retention_policies') | where('tenant = \''~tenant~'\' AND table_name = \''~table~'\'') | first %}
  {% set retention_days = policy.retention_days %}
  {% set archive_schema = policy.archive_schema %}

  {% set move_query %}
    INSERT INTO {{ archive_schema }}.archive_{{ table }}
    SELECT * FROM {{ this }}
    WHERE row_timestamp < DATEADD(day, -{{ retention_days }}, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP());

    DELETE FROM {{ this }}
    WHERE row_timestamp < DATEADD(day, -{{ retention_days }}, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP());
  {% endset %}

  {% do run_query(move_query) %}
{% endmacro %}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design per-tenant masking, macro-driven schema generation, and lineage tracking in dbt, while enforcing isolation and late data.

## Key Concepts
- Macro-driven per-tenant schemas
- Policy-based PII masking (redact, hash, partial)
- Global lineage table and dependency tracking
- Late-arrival handling and tenant isolation CI

## Code Example

```sql
-- macro: mask_pii
{% macro mask_pii(policy, field) -%}
  {% if policy == 'redact' -%}
    NULL
  {% elif policy == 'hash' -%}
    SHA2(CONCAT(COALESCE('{{tenant_id}}', 'global'), {{field}}), 256)
  {% else -%}
    {{ field }}
  {% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test masking across tenants with different policies?
- How would you extend lineage to support multi-tenant drift?
